I have find the definition of path_is_absolute() at [/src/basic/path-util.h](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/27a1719bbae776deb3fa6f4c39f29ddfb19efd38/src/basic/path-util.h#L43) 
It's very simple:
```C
static inline bool path_is_absolute(const char *p) {
        if (!p) /* A NULL pointer is definitely not an absolute path */
                return false;

        return p[0] == '/';
}
```
I don't know how it fails.
'path_is_absolute(p)' failed at src/basic/chase.c:566 might means [this line](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/27a1719bbae776deb3fa6f4c39f29ddfb19efd38/src/basic/chase.c#L584)
Not sure how to fix this

